   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Kinetic Warp\n\nA coarse mesh warp bends a whole word in staccato beats, one axis moving per keyframe.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A short, heavy display word needs a bold kinetic moment where the whole word bends and snaps instead of individual letters animating.\n- A rhythmic, beat-synced distortion: the mesh stops dead at every keyframe, so each pose lands like a drum hit.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a text entrance: the word is fully visible from frame 0 and only distorts. Use tracking-in or soft-blur-in.\n- The text is long or small: the mesh bends quarters of the frame, so use per-character-rise.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"STU\\nDIO\"\n- text_color (color): Text color, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- font_size (number, 40-200): Font size, default 107.1\n- layer_scale (number, 100-800): Layer scale, default 480\n- keyframe_stride (number, 5-40): Keyframe stride, default 20\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Kinetic Warp\n\n  A coarse mesh warp bends a whole word in staccato beats, one axis moving per keyframe.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/kinetic-warp/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"kinetic-warp\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Short, heavy display word. Use a line break to stack two lines.\", \"default\": \"STU\\nDIO\" },\n    { \"id\": \"text_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Color of the word.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Type size at a 100 % layer scale, in px at 1080 high.\", \"default\": 107.1, \"min\": 40, \"max\": 200, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"layer_scale\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Layer scale\", \"description\": \"Scale of the text layer in percent.\", \"default\": 480, \"min\": 100, \"max\": 800, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"%\" },\n    { \"id\": \"keyframe_stride\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Keyframe stride\", \"description\": \"Frames between warp poses (30 fps). Tune it to the beat.\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 5, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Kinetic Warp</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Passion+One:wght@400;700;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: \"Passion One\", Impact, sans-serif;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .kwp-canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n        .kwp-font { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; opacity: 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"kinetic-warp\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"kwp-clip\" class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0\">\n          <canvas id=\"kwp-canvas\" class=\"kwp-canvas\"></canvas>\n          <span class=\"kwp-font\" aria-hidden=\"true\">STUDIO</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function bz(id, a, b, c, d) {\n              return CustomEase.create(\"kwp-\" + id, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            // interpolate(frame, [a, b], [from, to], { easing }) as a tween (frames at 30 fps).\n            function tw(tl, el, from, to, a, b, ease, keep) {\n              var t = Object.assign({}, to, { duration: (b - a) / 30, ease: ease || \"none\", immediateRender: !keep });\n              tl.fromTo(el, from, t, a / 30);\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font size so it fits a fraction of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, frac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            function finish(tl) {\n              if (tl.duration() < TOTAL) tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"kinetic-warp\"] = tl;\n            }\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"STU\\nDIO\");\n            var textColor = str(vars.text_color, \"#FFFFFF\");\n            var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n            var sx = W / 1920, sy = H / 1080;\n            // Type scales with the frame height, but never wider than 1.8 x the width of a 1920 frame.\n            var u = Math.min(H / 1080, (W / 1920) * 1.8);\n            var scale = num(vars.layer_scale, 480, 100, 800) / 100;\n            var pxSize = num(vars.font_size, 107.1, 40, 200) * scale * u;\n            var pxLeading = 70 * scale * u;\n            var pxTracking = (-21 / 1000) * pxSize;\n            var stride = num(vars.keyframe_stride, 20, 5, 40);\n            var COLS = 4, ROWS = 2, STEP = 4;\n            var colRest = 960 * sx, colRight = 1255 * sx, colLeft = 678 * sx;\n            var rowRest = 540 * sy, rowDown = 850 * sy, rowUp = 387 * sy;\n            var FAMILY = '\"Passion One\", Impact, sans-serif';\n\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"kwp-canvas\");\n            canvas.width = W;\n            canvas.height = H;\n            var out = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n            var source = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n            source.width = W; source.height = H;\n            var mid = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n            mid.width = W; mid.height = H;\n            var midCtx = mid.getContext(\"2d\");\n\n            function drawSource() {\n              var c = source.getContext(\"2d\");\n              c.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              c.font = \"700 \" + pxSize + \"px \" + FAMILY;\n              c.letterSpacing = pxTracking + \"px\";\n              c.fillStyle = textColor;\n              c.textAlign = \"left\";\n              c.textBaseline = \"alphabetic\";\n              var lines = text.split(/\\\\n|\\n/);\n              var m = lines.map(function (l) { return c.measureText(l); });\n              var ascent = m[0].actualBoundingBoxAscent;\n              var descent = m[m.length - 1].actualBoundingBoxDescent;\n              var span = (lines.length - 1) * pxLeading;\n              var first = H / 2 - (span - ascent + descent) / 2;\n              lines.forEach(function (l, i) {\n                var x = W / 2 - (m[i].actualBoundingBoxRight - m[i].actualBoundingBoxLeft) / 2;\n                c.fillText(l, x, first + i * pxLeading);\n              });\n            }\n\n            // Monotone cubic interpolation through (xs, ys): the mesh bends smoothly without overshoot.\n            function monotone(xs, ys) {\n              var n = xs.length, h = [], d = [], m = [];\n              for (var i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) { h[i] = xs[i + 1] - xs[i]; d[i] = (ys[i + 1] - ys[i]) / h[i]; }\n              m[0] = d[0]; m[n - 1] = d[n - 2];\n              for (i = 1; i < n - 1; i++) m[i] = d[i - 1] * d[i] <= 0 ? 0 : (d[i - 1] + d[i]) / 2;\n              for (i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n                if (d[i] === 0) { m[i] = 0; m[i + 1] = 0; continue; }\n                var a = m[i] / d[i], b = m[i + 1] / d[i], s = a * a + b * b;\n                if (s > 9) { var k = 3 / Math.sqrt(s); m[i] = k * a * d[i]; m[i + 1] = k * b * d[i]; }\n              }\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= xs[0]) return ys[0] + m[0] * (x - xs[0]);\n                if (x >= xs[n - 1]) return ys[n - 1] + m[n - 1] * (x - xs[n - 1]);\n                var j = n - 2;\n                while (j > 0 && x < xs[j]) j--;\n                var t = (x - xs[j]) / h[j], t2 = t * t, t3 = t2 * t;\n                return (2 * t3 - 3 * t2 + 1) * ys[j] + (t3 - 2 * t2 + t) * h[j] * m[j] + (-2 * t3 + 3 * t2) * ys[j + 1] + (t3 - t2) * h[j] * m[j + 1];\n              };\n            }\n            var ease = bz(\"beat\", 0.3, 0.74, 0.09, 1);\n            // Six poses, one every `stride` frames; every segment eases on its own.\n            function pose(f, values) {\n              var seg = Math.min(4, Math.max(0, Math.floor(f / stride)));\n              var p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - seg * stride) / stride));\n              return values[seg] + (values[seg + 1] - values[seg]) * ease(p);\n            }\n            var P = { f: 0 };\n            function draw() {\n              var colX = pose(P.f, [colRest, colRight, colRight, colLeft, colLeft, colRest]);\n              var rowY = pose(P.f, [rowRest, rowRest, rowDown, rowDown, rowUp, rowRest]);\n              var xs = [], ys = [];\n              for (var i = 0; i <= COLS; i++) xs.push((i * W) / COLS);\n              for (i = 0; i <= ROWS; i++) ys.push((i * H) / ROWS);\n              var xd = xs.slice(), yd = ys.slice();\n              xd[Math.round(COLS / 2)] = colX;\n              yd[Math.round(ROWS / 2)] = rowY;\n              var gx = monotone(xd, xs), gy = monotone(yd, ys);\n              midCtx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              out.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              for (var d0 = 0; d0 < W; d0 += STEP) {\n                var d1 = Math.min(d0 + STEP, W), s0 = gx(d0), sw = gx(d1) - s0;\n                if (sw <= 0) continue;\n                midCtx.drawImage(source, s0, 0, sw, H, d0, 0, d1 - d0, H);\n              }\n              for (d0 = 0; d0 < H; d0 += STEP) {\n                d1 = Math.min(d0 + STEP, H);\n                s0 = gy(d0);\n                var sh = gy(d1) - s0;\n                if (sh <= 0) continue;\n                out.drawImage(mid, 0, s0, W, sh, 0, d0, W, d1 - d0);\n              }\n            }\n            drawSource();\n            draw();\n            // Redraw the source once the web font is in.\n            function refresh() { drawSource(); draw(); }\n            if (document.fonts) {\n              document.fonts.load(\"700 \" + pxSize + 'px \"Passion One\"').then(refresh, function () {});\n              document.fonts.ready.then(refresh, function () {});\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(P, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: draw }, 0);\n            finish(tl);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
